  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Loud sounds come from inside the underwater formation. Gaps spread into a huge crack. Shen Cong Sheng shouts, suppresses the effect of regret Gu, and attacks the crack with the immortal killer move Grand Collision. The formation breaks. The sealed demonic immortal flies out like a black arrow. Shen Cong Sheng flies closer and calls him Ancestor Shen Shang, saying he is a descendant of Shen clan and his junior.",
      "chapters": [
        1905
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_shen_cong_sheng",
        "gu_regret_gu",
        "move_grand_collision",
        "fac_shen_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He wears a tattered grey robe. His face is pale, his hair is messy, and his eyes are bloodshot and red.",
      "chapters": [
        1906
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Shen Cong Sheng’s true motive in coming was to save this ancestor. Shen Shang was the most outstanding Gu Immortal in Shen clan. When he was still rank six, a wisdom path rank eight great expert had called him the hundreds of years eastern immortal leader, with half of a venerable’s talent: he would lead Eastern Sea’s immortals in hundreds of years once he reached rank eight. He pursued strength, fell into the demonic path, and committed heinous deeds. The clan punished him lightly and kept protecting him. He stayed a righteous path Gu Immortal on the surface while acting like a demon. Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable suppressed him without exposing his identity. Shen clan announced that he had died from his tribulation.",
      "chapters": [
        1906
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "clan-standing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "reg_eastern_sea",
        "char_paradise_earth_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He floats in the air with a hoarse voice, even more coarse than crows. He wears a tattered grey robe. His face is pale, his hair is messy, and his eyes are bloodshot. Peak rank eight aura radiates from his body. He asks what year it is, sighs that Lord Paradise Earth died after all, and cups his fists at the other immortals. Shen Cong Sheng is already rank eight. With Shen Shang free, Shen clan would be the only Eastern Sea righteous path super force with two rank eight Gu Immortals.",
      "chapters": [
        1906
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "clan-standing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_eastern_sea_righteous_path"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is not restricted by the Merit Obelisk the way the others are. He opens his mouth and shoots a blood colored sound wave that collapses a supplementary formation at once. Shen Cong Sheng knows the inside details: Shen Shang did not cultivate sound path primarily, and that sound path method was not his true strength.",
      "chapters": [
        1906
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "clan-standing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_merit_obelisk"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "His hair is messy, his eyes are bloodshot, and his face is distorted. Black fire burns on his body while he drools and waves his limbs.",
      "chapters": [
        1908
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "madness",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the heavenly spine he tells Shen Cong Sheng he will hand over his human path inheritance for the clan’s benefit, as repayment of a debt he owed them. He will not pass the human path Immortal Gu, because he has to keep using them. What he passes is cultivation experience, killer moves, and Immortal Gu recipes. His memory is fragmented. He used to major in sound path. After he refined heal injury Immortal Gu, he saw hope of human path. In order to convert to human path, he did many things in secret against the rules of the righteous path. His clan defended him and covered those incidents, but he could not hide them from Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable. Paradise Earth did not kill him. Because he had spent years saving lives and helping the injured, Paradise Earth gave him a chance to redeem himself, and promised that if he seized it he might successfully convert. He then cultivated in the underwater formation Paradise Earth had set up.",
      "chapters": [
        1915
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "heavenly-spine-talk",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "sys_gu_recipe",
        "gu_heal_injury_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "With heal injury Immortal Gu as the foundation he developed saving dead healing injuries, light injuries, heavy injuries, fatal injuries, sensory injuries, seven laborious injuries, and other killer moves. He then created the killer move countless injury marks, deduced the Immortal Gu recipe of injury mark Immortal Gu from it, refined that Gu, and replaced his vital Gu. Attacks that damage him convert into injury marks, and more of those marks raise the power of mutual injuries, which he names as his main offensive method. Injury mark Immortal Gu is the core of that inheritance. He laughs that he is afraid he will not be able to take the path further, and tells Shen Cong Sheng to switch to human path if interested, or to choose a successor.",
      "chapters": [
        1915
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "heavenly-spine-talk",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_injury_mark_immortal_gu",
        "sys_vital_gu"
      ]
    }
  ],
